CHD_250312_011.webp A single-story cave-inspired container house design measuring 5.91m in length, 2.33m in width, and 2.37m in height. The building facade features a dramatic contrast: rugged, torn-like concrete slab edges juxtaposed against a smooth, reflective central surface. Massive, rough-textured concrete elements stand like vertical bookends, framing the towering glass and metal entrance. At the street level, the entrance and lower facade are wrapped in a warm metal finish, likely brass or brass-colored metal, exuding a luxurious feel under the light. Behind the raw concrete slabs, a glass curtain wall creates a modern, light-filled central space. The background features an urban setting with moody lighting, emphasizing the raw, industrial aesthetic.
